WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.012
Privacy — which is where a data
architect earns trust with HR.

2
00:00:04.012 --> 00:00:09.188
Moving HR attributes into a directory
is a disclosure of personnel records.

3
00:00:09.188 --> 00:00:15.303
So: confirm the routine-use basis under
the governing system-of-records notices —

4
00:00:15.303 --> 00:00:18.453
OPM/GOVT-1 for general personnel records,

5
00:00:18.453 --> 00:00:21.788
plus the agency's own —
before anything flows.

6
00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:26.587
Minimize: send only attributes an
identity decision actually reads,

7
00:00:26.587 --> 00:00:31.050
as codes rather than narrative, and
never use the SSN as a join key.

8
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:35.600
Update the privacy impact assessment
for the new flow and its consumers.

9
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.095
And protect the flow: encrypt every leg,

10
00:00:38.095 --> 00:00:43.162
and keep logs to the person key and a
payload hash rather than the record itself.

11
00:00:43.162 --> 00:00:47.407
The principle underneath: HR
remains the system of records;

12
00:00:47.407 --> 00:00:53.076
identity is a governed consumer that
never writes an HR-mastered fact back.
